{
  "id": "05751_senbou",
  "headword": "{羨望|せんぼう}",
  "reading": "せんぼう",
  "part_of_speech": "noun, suru verb",
  "gloss": "envy; admiration with desire",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "envy; admiration with desire",
      "explanation": "A feeling of wanting what someone else has; admiring while wishing to possess the same qualities or things."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "05751_senbou_ex1",
      "japanese": "{彼|かれ}の{才能|さいのう}に{羨望|せんぼう}を{感|かん}じる。",
      "english": "I feel envy at his talent.",
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "05751_senbou_ex2",
      "japanese": "{羨望|せんぼう}の{眼差|まなざ}しで{見|み}られる。",
      "english": "To be looked at with envious eyes.",
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "05751_senbou_ex3",
      "japanese": "{彼女|かのじょ}の{成功|せいこう}は{皆|みな}の{羨望|せんぼう}の{的|まと}だ。",
      "english": "Her success is the object of everyone's envy.",
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    }
  ],
  "notes": "NUANCE:\n{羨望|せんぼう} can be positive (admiration mixed with desire) or negative (jealousy). It's more literary than {嫉妬|しっと} (jealousy).\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {羨望|せんぼう}の{的|まと}: object of envy\n- {羨望|せんぼう}の{眼差|まなざ}し: envious gaze\n- {羨望|せんぼう}を{抱|いだ}く: to harbor envy\n- {羨望|せんぼう}に{値|あたい}する: to be worthy of envy\n\nRELATED TERMS:\n- {嫉妬|しっと}: jealousy (stronger, more negative)\n- {羨|うらや}ましい: enviable\n- {憧|あこが}れ: longing, admiration",
